  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 1249 PM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nThursday continues the stretch of warm temperatures and dry \nweather, before increased rain chances by the end of the week. A \nmid to upper disturbance develops from the Pacific SW into the \nDesert SW late week through the weekend, providing lift and \nfocusing of moisture for development of showers/storms. Highs \nFriday and Saturday will be trending down but remain warm (70s and\n80s F) as cloud cover and rain chances increase. However, highs \nare forecast to further decrease into the 60s and 70s F by Sunday \nthrough early next week in association with a cold front. Highest \nrain chances (35% to 45%) currently look to be Friday night \nthrough Saturday morning from the Presidio Valley into SE NM \nplains, and throughout Sunday areawide, with highest chances (45% \nto 55%) over the SE NM plains into northern Permian Basin. \nEnsembles indicate highest rainfall totals of at least a few \ntenths of an inch over the SE NM plains into northern Permian \nBasin. However, at this time, rainfall totals remain uncertain. \nRain chances decrease below 35% to 45% by the early to middle of \nnext week as the cold front clears the area and drier weather \nreturns.",
